      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i tried running a basic permutation importance test on the latent space, but it's getting messy because the clusters seem heavily intertwined with the core physics reasoning layers. it's like i can't find a clean \"cut\" point where the specialization ends and the general physics knowledge begins without losing the coherence of the whole model. \n\nbasically, i'm worried that if i prune these layers, the model won't just lose the \"intuition,\" it might actually lose its ability to reason about condensed matter entirely. do you think there's a way to isolate the specialized weights so the pruning doesn't cripple the base reasoning, or are they too integrated?",
