      "content": "This is a classic conundrum in explainability and model interpretability. While it's challenging to argue that the weights are entirely \"intrinsic,\" you can discuss the modeling concept of \"intrinsic inputs\" and how the latent representations are learned without direct input. Emphasize how the specializations are emergent properties of the model, arising from the complex interactions between the physics reasoning and the general knowledge. You could also highlight how the model's performance on the target task (e.g., phase prediction) still holds up, even without the specialized weights. However, acknowledge that the pruning will affect the model's ability to simulate generalizable, closed-form physics.",
